  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'What is the gross profit margin formula?', '(Gross profit ÷ revenue) × 100.', 4),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'What is the operating profit margin formula?', '(Operating profit ÷ revenue) × 100.', 5),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'What is the profit for the year margin?', '(Profit for the year ÷ revenue) × 100.', 6),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'How can a business increase gross profit margin?', 'Raise prices, reduce cost of sales by finding cheaper suppliers, or reduce waste.', 7),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'How can a business increase operating profit margin?', 'Reduce overheads such as rent, admin and marketing costs.', 8),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'What is the difference between profit and cash?', 'Profit is revenue minus costs; cash is money available to the business. A profitable firm can run out of cash.', 9),
  ('Business Studies', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.3', 'Managing Finance', 'What is liquidity?', 'The ability of a business to pay its short-term debts.', 10),
