  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.4', 'Relations Between the Branches', 'What is the separation of powers?', 'The division of government into legislative, executive and judicial branches, each checking the others.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is the core idea of anarchism?', 'The rejection of the state and all forms of coercive authority.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is collectivist anarchism?', 'Anarchism based on common ownership and cooperation, e.g. anarcho-communism and anarcho-syndicalism.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is individualist anarchism?', 'Anarchism prioritising individual sovereignty and rejecting the state, e.g. anarcho-capitalism and egoism.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is anarcho-communism?', 'A stateless society with common ownership and distribution according to need.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is anarcho-syndicalism?', 'Anarchism using trade unions and general strikes to overthrow capitalism and the state.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is anarcho-capitalism?', 'The belief that the free market can replace the state entirely, including provision of security and justice.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is egoism?', 'Stirner''s belief that individuals should act solely in their own interest, rejecting all external authority.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is Stirner''s contribution to anarchism?', 'He argued the individual ego is supreme, and rejected the state, morality and religion.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is Goldman''s contribution to anarchism?', 'She linked anarchism with feminism and opposed the state, religion and marriage as oppressive.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of human nature?', 'Humans are naturally sociable and cooperative (collectivists) or rational and self-interested (individualists).', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of the economy?', 'Collectivists want common ownership; individualists want free markets without the state.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of the state?', 'The state is coercive, corrupting and unnecessary.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '2.5', 'Anarchism', 'What is the anarchist view of society?', 'Society can organise itself naturally without the state.', 13),
