  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is the Bill of Rights?', 'The first ten amendments to the US Constitution, protecting individual rights.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is the First Amendment?', 'Freedom of religion, speech, press, assembly and petition.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is the Second Amendment?', 'The right to keep and bear arms.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is the Fourteenth Amendment?', 'It guarantees equal protection of the laws and due process to all citizens.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'How is the US Constitution amended?', 'Proposed by two-thirds of both houses of Congress (or a convention called by two-thirds of states), and ratified by three-quarters of the states.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'How many amendments have there been?', '27, the last being ratified in 1992.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is the separation of powers in the US?', 'Legislative power with Congress, executive power with the President, and judicial power with the courts.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is federalism?', 'Power is shared between the federal government and the states.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is dual federalism?', 'Federal and state governments operate in separate spheres (the "layer cake" model).', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is cooperative federalism?', 'Federal and state governments work together, e.g. through grants (the "marble cake" model).', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is new federalism?', 'Returning power to the states, associated with Nixon and Reagan.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.1', 'US Constitution and Federalism', 'What is the Commerce Clause?', 'It gives Congress power to regulate interstate commerce, used to expand federal power.', 15),
