  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is the role of the Senate Majority Leader?', 'The leader of the majority party in the Senate, controlling the floor agenda.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is a standing committee?', 'A permanent committee that scrutinises legislation and oversees policy areas.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is the House Rules Committee?', 'It sets the terms of debate for bills in the House.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is the role of Congress in oversight?', 'Investigating and scrutinising the executive through hearings and investigations.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is the confirmation power of the Senate?', 'The Senate must approve presidential appointments, including Supreme Court justices and Cabinet members.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is the treaty ratification power?', 'Treaties require approval by two-thirds of the Senate.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is impeachment?', 'The House can impeach (charge) federal officials; the Senate tries them, and removal requires a two-thirds vote.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'How many times has a President been impeached?', 'Three presidents, four impeachments: Andrew Johnson (1868), Clinton (1998) and Trump (2019 and 2021). None was removed by the Senate.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is partisanship in Congress?', 'Members voting along party lines; it has increased greatly in recent decades.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is gridlock?', 'When Congress and the President fail to pass legislation because of divided government or partisanship.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is divided government?', 'When one party controls the presidency and the other controls one or both houses of Congress.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is representation in Congress?', 'Members represent their constituents, parties and interest groups.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is pork-barrel politics?', 'Spending targeted at a member''s district to gain support.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.2', 'US Congress', 'What is the significance of incumbency?', 'Incumbents have very high re-election rates due to name recognition, funding and constituency service.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What are the formal powers of the President?', 'Commander-in-chief, proposing legislation, veto, appointments, treaties, pardons and executing laws.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What are the informal powers of the President?', 'Persuasion, the electoral mandate, the bully pulpit, and executive orders.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the power to persuade?', 'Neustadt''s argument that the President''s real power lies in persuading others.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is an executive order?', 'A directive issued by the President to manage the federal government, without congressional approval.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is a signing statement?', 'A statement issued by the President when signing a bill, which may interpret or challenge parts of it.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the Executive Office of the President?', 'The agencies that support the President, including the White House Office and the Office of Management and Budget.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the Cabinet in the US?', 'The heads of the executive departments, who advise the President but have no collective responsibility.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the bully pulpit?', 'The President''s platform to speak directly to the public and influence opinion.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the imperial presidency?', 'Schlesinger''s idea that the President has become too powerful, especially in foreign policy.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the imperilled presidency?', 'The idea that the President is too weak because of constraints from Congress, courts and media.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What are the constraints on the President?', 'Congress, the Supreme Court, the Constitution, federalism, public opinion and the media.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the War Powers Resolution 1973?', 'It requires the President to notify Congress within 48 hours of deploying troops and limits deployments to 60 days without approval.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the role of the Vice President?', 'President of the Senate with a tie-breaking vote, and first in line to succeed the President.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the 25th Amendment?', 'It sets out procedures for presidential succession and disability.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is a lame duck President?', 'A President in the final period of office, often with reduced power.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the honeymoon period?', 'The early period of a presidency when the President has high approval and can achieve more.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the role of the President in foreign policy?', 'Commander-in-chief, negotiating treaties, appointing ambassadors, and leading diplomacy.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is executive privilege?', 'The President''s claim to withhold information from Congress and the courts, limited by US v Nixon (1974).', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the significance of US v Nixon (1974)?', 'The Supreme Court ruled the President must hand over the Watergate tapes, limiting executive privilege.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is the unitary executive theory?', 'The view that the President has complete control over the executive branch.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is a presidential mandate?', 'The authority to carry out policies based on winning an election.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.3', 'US Presidency', 'What is presidential approval rating?', 'A measure of public support for the President, which affects their power.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is judicial review in the US?', 'The power of courts to declare laws and executive actions unconstitutional.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is the Supreme Court''s composition?', 'Nine justices appointed for life by the President and confirmed by the Senate.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is judicial activism?', 'When judges actively interpret the Constitution to shape policy.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is judicial restraint?', 'When judges defer to elected branches and follow precedent.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is originalism?', 'Interpreting the Constitution according to its original meaning.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is the living constitution?', 'Interpreting the Constitution in light of current values.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is stare decisis?', 'Following precedent in judicial decisions.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was Brown v Board of Education (1954)?', 'It ruled racial segregation in public schools unconstitutional.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was Roe v Wade (1973)?', 'It established a constitutional right to abortion.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was Dobbs v Jackson (2022)?', 'It overturned Roe v Wade, returning abortion regulation to the states.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was Obergefell v Hodges (2015)?', 'It legalised same-sex marriage nationwide.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was DC v Heller (2008)?', 'It ruled the Second Amendment protects an individual right to own firearms.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was Students for Fair Admissions v Harvard (2023)?', 'It ruled race-conscious affirmative action in college admissions unconstitutional.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is a swing justice?', 'A justice whose vote often decides close cases, e.g. Anthony Kennedy.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is the politicisation of the Supreme Court?', 'The perception that justices vote along ideological lines and that appointments are highly partisan.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was the controversy over the Garland nomination (2016)?', 'The Republican Senate refused to hold hearings for Obama''s nominee, Merrick Garland.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is the current ideological balance of the Supreme Court?', 'A 6–3 conservative majority following Trump''s three appointments.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is the civil rights movement?', 'The struggle for equal rights for African Americans, especially in the 1950s and 60s.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was the Civil Rights Act 1964?', 'It banned discrimination based on race, colour, religion, sex or national origin.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was the Voting Rights Act 1965?', 'It outlawed discriminatory voting practices such as literacy tests.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What was Shelby County v Holder (2013)?', 'It struck down a key part of the Voting Rights Act requiring federal pre-clearance for some states.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.4', 'US Supreme Court and Civil Rights', 'What is affirmative action?', 'Policies giving preferential treatment to disadvantaged groups to address past discrimination.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the presidential election process?', 'Invisible primary, primaries and caucuses, national conventions, the general election campaign, and the Electoral College vote.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the Electoral College?', '538 electors allocated to states based on congressional representation; a candidate needs 270 to win.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is winner-takes-all?', 'In most states, the candidate with the most votes wins all the state''s electoral votes.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'Which states don''t use winner-takes-all?', 'Maine and Nebraska allocate some electoral votes by congressional district.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is a swing state?', 'A state where either party could win, e.g. Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is a national convention?', 'A party meeting that formally nominates its presidential candidate and adopts a platform.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the significance of Super Tuesday?', 'The day when many states hold primaries, often decisive in the nomination race.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is campaign finance?', 'The funding of election campaigns, regulated by law.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is a Super PAC?', 'A political action committee that can raise and spend unlimited amounts, but can''t coordinate directly with campaigns.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is soft money?', 'Money donated to parties for general activities rather than specific candidates, restricted by the Bipartisan Campaign Reform Act 2002.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the role of interest groups in the US?', 'They lobby Congress and the executive, fund campaigns and bring legal cases.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the NRA?', 'The National Rifle Association, an influential interest group defending gun rights.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is lobbying?', 'Attempting to influence legislators and officials on behalf of interest groups.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the revolving door?', 'Movement of people between government and lobbying roles.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What are the two main parties in the US?', 'The Democrats (liberal) and the Republicans (conservative).', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is party polarisation?', 'Parties moving further apart ideologically, with fewer moderates.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the role of third parties?', 'They can influence debate and act as spoilers, e.g. Ralph Nader in 2000.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is voter turnout in US elections?', 'Relatively low compared with other democracies, especially in midterms.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the midterm election?', 'Elections held halfway through a presidential term, for all House seats and a third of the Senate.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What factors influence voting in the US?', 'Race, religion, gender, education, age, region and the economy.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is voter ID laws'' impact?', 'Critics argue they suppress minority turnout; supporters say they prevent fraud.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.5', 'US Democracy and Participation', 'What is the significance of the 2020 election?', 'Biden won, and Trump''s refusal to accept the result led to the 6 January 2021 Capitol attack.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the rational approach to comparative politics?', 'It explains outcomes by the self-interested choices of individuals.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the cultural approach to comparative politics?', 'It explains outcomes by shared values, beliefs and norms.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the structural approach?', 'It explains outcomes by institutions and the rules that shape behaviour.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do the UK and US constitutions differ?', 'The UK''s is uncodified, unentrenched and unitary; the US''s is codified, entrenched and federal.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do the UK and US legislatures differ?', 'Congress has more power over legislation and appointments; the UK Parliament is dominated by the executive.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do the UK and US executives differ?', 'The US President is elected separately with fixed terms; the UK PM depends on parliamentary support.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do the UK and US Supreme Courts differ?', 'The US Court can strike down laws; the UK Court can''t overturn Acts of Parliament.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How are rights protected in the UK and US?', 'The US has an entrenched Bill of Rights; the UK relies on the Human Rights Act, which Parliament can amend.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do UK and US parties differ?', 'UK parties are more centralised and disciplined; US parties are decentralised and candidate-centred.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do UK and US pressure groups differ?', 'US groups have more access points and influence, including through the courts and campaign finance.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How does federalism compare with devolution?', 'Federalism is constitutionally entrenched; devolution can in theory be revoked by Westminster.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How does the separation of powers compare?', 'The US has a strict separation; the UK has a fusion of executive and legislature.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'Why do US legislators rebel more often than UK MPs?', 'Weaker party discipline, separate elections, and primaries make members more responsive to constituents.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do the UK and US differ in their elections?', 'The US has fixed terms, primaries and the Electoral College; the UK has flexible elections and party selection.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'How do the UK and US differ in campaign finance?', 'US spending is much higher with fewer limits; the UK has strict spending limits and bans paid political TV ads.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the cultural explanation for gun control differences?', 'The US has a strong gun culture linked to history and the Second Amendment.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'Why is the US Supreme Court more powerful than the UK''s?', 'The codified, entrenched constitution gives the US Court power to overturn laws.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the rational explanation for Senate filibusters?', 'Senators use filibusters strategically to block legislation they oppose.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the significance of structural differences in executive power?', 'The US President has constitutional independence; the UK PM''s power depends on parliamentary majority.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What are the similarities between the UK and US?', 'Both are liberal democracies with two-party dominance, FPTP elections and independent judiciaries.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'What is the convergence thesis?', 'The idea that UK and US politics are becoming more similar, e.g. presidentialisation of UK PMs.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3A.6', 'Comparative Approaches', 'Why might convergence be limited?', 'Fundamental constitutional and institutional differences remain.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the state?', 'A political entity with sovereignty over a defined territory and population.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is national sovereignty?', 'A state''s supreme authority within its territory and independence from external control.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is a nation-state?', 'A state whose population shares a common national identity.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is globalisation?', 'The growing interconnectedness of states through economic, political and cultural flows.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is economic globalisation?', 'The integration of national economies through trade, investment and financial flows.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is political globalisation?', 'The growth of international organisations and cooperation beyond the state.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is cultural globalisation?', 'The spread of cultural ideas, products and values across borders.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the hyperglobalist view?', 'Globalisation has made states less relevant, creating a borderless world.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the sceptical view?', 'States remain powerful and globalisation is exaggerated.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the transformationalist view?', 'Globalisation is transforming states and power, but states remain important.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the impact of globalisation on sovereignty?', 'States have less control over their economies, borders and policies.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the role of MNCs in globalisation?', 'They drive global trade and investment and can influence states.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the Washington Consensus?', 'Free-market policies promoted by the IMF, World Bank and US Treasury.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is humanitarian intervention?', 'Military intervention in another state to protect human rights.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the impact of globalisation on inequality?', 'It has lifted many out of poverty but increased inequality within some states.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is anti-globalisation?', 'Movements opposing globalisation''s economic, cultural and environmental impacts.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the impact of globalisation on the environment?', 'Increased emissions and resource use, but also international cooperation on environmental issues.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the impact of globalisation on culture?', 'Cultural homogenisation, but also hybridisation and local resistance.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the digital revolution''s impact on globalisation?', 'Faster communication and information flows, e-commerce and social media across borders.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the role of global civil society?', 'NGOs and social movements that act across borders to influence global issues.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is the impact of globalisation on democracy?', 'It can spread democratic ideas but may reduce national democratic control.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.1', 'The State and Globalisation', 'What is deglobalisation?', 'A reduction in global integration, e.g. more protectionism after 2008 and COVID-19.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the United Nations?', 'An international organisation founded in 1945 to maintain peace and security and promote cooperation.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the UN Security Council?', 'The UN body responsible for international peace and security, with 5 permanent members and 10 elected members.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'Who are the P5?', 'The USA, the UK, France, Russia and China, each with a veto.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the UN General Assembly?', 'The UN''s main deliberative body, where all 193 members have one vote.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the International Monetary Fund?', 'An organisation promoting financial stability and providing loans to countries in crisis.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the World Bank?', 'An organisation providing loans and grants for development projects.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the World Trade Organization?', 'An organisation promoting free trade and settling trade disputes.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the G7?', 'A group of seven major advanced economies: USA, UK, France, Germany, Italy, Canada and Japan.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the G20?', 'A group of 19 major economies plus the EU (and the African Union since 2023), discussing global economic issues.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is NATO?', 'The North Atlantic Treaty Organization, a military alliance founded in 1949 for collective defence.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is conditionality?', 'Conditions attached to IMF and World Bank loans, e.g. economic reforms.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What are structural adjustment programmes?', 'IMF and World Bank programmes requiring market reforms in exchange for loans.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the North–South divide?', 'The economic gap between wealthy developed countries and poorer developing countries.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the Millennium Development Goals?', 'Eight UN goals set in 2000 to reduce poverty and improve development by 2015.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the Sustainable Development Goals?', '17 UN goals set in 2015 to achieve sustainable development by 2030.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What are the criticisms of the UN Security Council?', 'The veto causes deadlock, and membership reflects 1945 power rather than today''s.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the role of NATO in global security?', 'Collective defence, crisis management and cooperative security.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is NATO expansion?', 'The growth of NATO membership, including Finland (2023) and Sweden (2024).', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the role of the WTO in trade disputes?', 'Its dispute settlement mechanism resolves trade conflicts between members.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is the Doha Round?', 'WTO trade negotiations started in 2001 that failed to reach agreement.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is economic governance?', 'The international institutions and rules governing the global economy.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.2', 'Global Governance: Political and Economic', 'What is political governance?', 'The international institutions and rules governing peace and security.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the Universal Declaration of Human Rights?', 'A 1948 UN declaration setting out fundamental human rights.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the International Court of Justice?', 'The UN''s principal judicial body, settling disputes between states.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the International Criminal Court?', 'A court that prosecutes individuals for genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the European Court of Human Rights?', 'A court enforcing the European Convention on Human Rights.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the Responsibility to Protect?', 'A 2005 UN principle that states must protect their populations, and the international community should intervene if they fail.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is humanitarian intervention?', 'Military intervention to prevent human rights abuses.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'Give an example of successful humanitarian intervention.', 'Sierra Leone (2000), where UK intervention helped end the civil war.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'Give an example of unsuccessful humanitarian intervention.', 'Libya (2011), which removed Gaddafi but led to instability and civil war.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the Rwandan genocide (1994)?', 'The mass killing of Tutsis, which the international community failed to prevent.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What are the limits of the ICC?', 'Major powers, including the US, China and Russia, are not members; it relies on state cooperation.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is global environmental governance?', 'International institutions and agreements addressing environmental issues.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the Kyoto Protocol (1997)?', 'An agreement setting binding emissions targets for developed countries.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the Paris Agreement (2015)?', 'An agreement to limit global warming to well below 2°C, with nationally determined contributions.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is COP?', 'Conference of the Parties, the annual UN climate change conference.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change?', 'The UN body assessing scientific evidence on climate change.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the tragedy of the commons in global politics?', 'Shared resources are overused because no single state has an incentive to limit its use.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the North–South divide on climate change?', 'Developing countries argue developed countries caused the problem and should bear more of the cost.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What are the limits of global environmental governance?', 'Lack of enforcement, national interests and free-riding.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is common but differentiated responsibility?', 'All states share responsibility for climate change, but developed states have greater responsibility.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the role of NGOs in human rights?', 'They monitor abuses, campaign, and provide evidence, e.g. Amnesty International and Human Rights Watch.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is state sovereignty''s conflict with human rights?', 'Intervention to protect rights may violate a state''s sovereignty.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.3', 'Global Governance: Human Rights and Environmental', 'What is the significance of the Glasgow COP26 (2021)?', 'It agreed to "phase down" coal and strengthen emissions targets.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is hard power?', 'The use of military and economic force to influence others.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is soft power?', 'The ability to influence others through attraction, culture and values.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is smart power?', 'The combination of hard and soft power.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is a superpower?', 'A state with global influence across economic, military and cultural areas.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is a great power?', 'A state with significant influence, but less than a superpower.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is an emerging power?', 'A state whose power is growing, e.g. India and Brazil.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is unipolarity?', 'A world dominated by one superpower, e.g. the USA after the Cold War.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is bipolarity?', 'A world dominated by two superpowers, e.g. the USA and USSR during the Cold War.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is multipolarity?', 'A world with several centres of power.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is the rise of China?', 'China''s growing economic, military and diplomatic power.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is the Belt and Road Initiative?', 'China''s global infrastructure investment programme to increase its influence.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is the role of Russia in global politics?', 'A nuclear power and P5 member, asserting influence through military action, e.g. the invasion of Ukraine.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is a failed state?', 'A state unable to provide basic services or maintain control of its territory.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is a rogue state?', 'A state seen as a threat to world peace, e.g. North Korea.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is democratisation?', 'The spread of democracy to more states.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is the democratic peace theory?', 'Democracies rarely go to war with each other.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is authoritarianism?', 'A system of government with concentrated power and limited political freedom.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is a semi-democratic state?', 'A state with some democratic features but significant restrictions on freedoms.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is development and its measurement?', 'Improvement in living standards, measured by GDP per capita, HDI and other indicators.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is the significance of BRICS?', 'A group of emerging economies (Brazil, Russia, India, China, South Africa and new members) challenging Western dominance.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is the Thucydides Trap?', 'The idea that war is likely when a rising power challenges an established power, e.g. the US and China.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.4', 'Power and Developments', 'What is polarity''s effect on global stability?', 'Realists argue bipolarity is most stable; others argue unipolarity or multipolarity can be stable.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is regionalism?', 'Cooperation and integration between states in a geographic region.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is economic regionalism?', 'Regional economic cooperation, e.g. free trade areas.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is security regionalism?', 'Regional cooperation on security issues.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is political regionalism?', 'Regional political cooperation and integration.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the European Union?', 'A political and economic union of 27 European states.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the European Commission?', 'The EU''s executive body, proposing legislation and enforcing EU law.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the European Parliament?', 'The EU''s directly elected legislative body.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the Council of the European Union?', 'The body representing member state governments, sharing legislative power with the Parliament.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the European Council?', 'The body of heads of state or government that sets the EU''s overall direction.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the Court of Justice of the EU?', 'The court interpreting EU law and ensuring its uniform application.', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the single market?', 'Free movement of goods, services, capital and people within the EU.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the eurozone?', 'EU member states that use the euro as their currency.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What was the Maastricht Treaty (1992)?', 'It created the EU, European citizenship and the path to the euro.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What was the Lisbon Treaty (2007)?', 'It reformed EU institutions and created Article 50 for leaving the EU.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is widening?', 'Increasing the number of EU member states.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is deepening?', 'Increasing integration between existing member states.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is supranationalism?', 'Decision-making above the level of the state, with binding authority.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is intergovernmentalism?', 'Cooperation between states where each retains sovereignty.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is ASEAN?', 'The Association of Southeast Asian Nations, promoting regional cooperation.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the African Union?', 'An organisation promoting unity and cooperation among African states.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the eurozone crisis?', 'The debt crisis from 2009 affecting countries such as Greece, revealing flaws in monetary union without fiscal union.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.5', 'Regionalism and the EU', 'What is the impact of Brexit on the EU?', 'Loss of a major member, but the EU remained united in negotiations.', 22),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is realism?', 'A theory that states are the main actors in an anarchic international system, pursuing power and security.', 1),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is liberalism in global politics?', 'A theory that cooperation between states is possible through institutions, trade and democracy.', 2),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is anarchy in international relations?', 'The absence of a central authority above states.', 3),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the security dilemma?', 'When one state increases its security, others feel threatened and respond, leading to insecurity.', 4),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the balance of power?', 'States form alliances to prevent any one state from becoming too powerful.', 5),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is complex interdependence?', 'The liberal idea that states are linked by many connections, making conflict costly.', 6),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is global governance?', 'Cooperation between states and international organisations to manage global issues.', 7),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is constructivism?', 'A theory that international relations are shaped by ideas, identities and norms.', 8),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is neorealism?', 'A version of realism emphasising the structure of the international system rather than human nature.', 9),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is classical realism?', 'A version of realism emphasising human nature as the cause of state behaviour (Morgenthau).', 10),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is neoliberal institutionalism?', 'A liberal theory arguing institutions help states cooperate by reducing uncertainty.', 11),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the realist view of human nature?', 'Humans are selfish and power-seeking.', 12),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the liberal view of human nature?', 'Humans are capable of cooperation and progress.', 13),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the realist view of the state?', 'States are the main actors and pursue national interests.', 14),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the liberal view of international organisations?', 'They promote cooperation, peace and shared norms.', 15),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the realist view of international organisations?', 'They reflect the interests of powerful states and have limited independent influence.', 16),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the liberal view of war?', 'War can be prevented through democracy, trade and institutions.', 17),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the realist view of war?', 'War is inevitable in an anarchic system.', 18),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the significance of the 2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine for realism?', 'It supports realist views of power politics and the limits of international institutions.', 19),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the significance of the EU for liberalism?', 'It shows that cooperation and integration can bring peace between former enemies.', 20),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the English School?', 'A theory that states form an international society with shared rules and norms.', 21),
  ('Politics', 'Edexcel', 'alevel', '3B.6', 'Comparative Theories', 'What is the relevance of realism and liberalism today?', 'Both explain aspects of global politics: realism explains conflict and power; liberalism explains cooperation.', 22)
),
fresh AS (
  SELECT v.* FROM v
  WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM flashcards f
    WHERE f.subject = v.subject AND f.exam_board = v.exam_board AND f.level = v.level
      AND f.topic_id = v.topic_id AND f.front = v.front)
),
cur AS (
  SELECT subject, exam_board, level, topic_id, count(*) AS n, max(card_order) AS mx
  FROM flashcards
  WHERE subject = 'Politics' AND exam_board = 'Edexcel' AND level = 'alevel'
  GROUP BY 1, 2, 3, 4
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT fr.*, coalesce(c.n, 0) AS n, coalesce(c.mx, 0) AS mx,
         row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY fr.topic_id ORDER BY fr.ord) AS rn
  FROM fresh fr
  LEFT JOIN cur c USING (subject, exam_board, level, topic_id)
)
INSERT INTO flashcards (subject, exam_board, topic_id, topic_name, front, back, card_order, level)
SELECT subject, exam_board, topic_id, topic_name, front, back, mx + rn, level
FROM ranked
WHERE n + rn <= 30;

COMMIT;
